1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
AI models give in when you argue.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
EvidenceTune changes its answer only when the quoted evidence supports it.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
First, a historical comparison: plain training against EvidenceTune version six.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Shown a wrong quote, plain training asked for the source 80 times out of 272.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
EvidenceTune asked 208 times.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
In this chosen example, the quote is about returning copies, not rights.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Plain training switches.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
EvidenceTune holds.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The released model is a later merge, alpha point seven five.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:47,000
On frozen proxy tests, recorded, it passes 222 of 240 semantic rows and 253 of 270 targeted rows, against 213 and 247 for version seven.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Scope: synthetic proxy tests only.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Teacher labels had no human audit, by team decision.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
No safety, natural-text, Arabic, or general superiority claims.
